From 91ce4754fcc30d68e008da0e36dccbcbc0c79555 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 15:43:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 116/117] DOS-PORT: patch 0116 -- test hook to force the
 darkening path

DOSAGS_FORCE_DARKEN=<n> sets the ambient light level (play.rtint_*) at
start_game(), so the one path that actually needs the light table can be
made to run on demand.

Split out from the fix it exists to test, and deliberately applied FIRST,
so it is present in BOTH arms of that A/B. A hook that existed only in the
arm under test could not produce a comparison -- the same mistake made
with the per-call timing in the first 0113 draft, where the A arm could
not emit the metric the threshold was set on.

It sets the AMBIENT source rather than a region's Light, because that is
also the script-enables-it-later case, so it exercises the lazy hook
rather than the eager branch -- the harder of the two paths.

Honest note on what this does NOT achieve: on both available 8-bit
fixtures, forcing ambient darkening on still yields
"colormap_consumers transblend=0 litblend=0" over a whole 5000-tick run.
It makes the table get BUILT, proving the decision path, but no sprite in
either fixture is drawn through apply_tint_or_light, so the blend itself
still never executes. Exercising that needs content with a visible
character on a darkened region, which neither fixture has.
---
 Engine/main/game_start.cpp | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Engine/main/game_start.cpp b/Engine/main/game_start.cpp
index 0daf32606..dc3eb734e 100644
--- a/Engine/main/game_start.cpp
+++ b/Engine/main/game_start.cpp
@@ -121,6 +121,33 @@ void start_game()
     dos_port_startup_timing.preloop_game_start_script_ms = DOS_PORT_PRELOOP_MS(_dp_t0);
 #endif
 
+#ifdef __DJGPP__
+    // DOS-PORT patch 0116, TEST HOOK: force ambient darkening on.
+    //
+    // Patch 0116 stops building the light table when nothing can darken.
+    // That makes the darkening path -- the one case where the table is
+    // genuinely needed -- a path our correctness gate never executes:
+    // both 8-bit fixtures report colormap_consumers 0/0, so DOSBox-X
+    // cannot catch a mistake in it. This env var forces the path to run so
+    // the lazy build and the blend output can actually be compared
+    // against the eager build, instead of being argued about.
+    //
+    // Sets the AMBIENT source (play.rtint_*), which is also the
+    // script-enables-it-later case, so it exercises the lazy hook rather
+    // than the eager branch -- the harder of the two paths.
+    {
+        const char *force_dark = getenv("DOSAGS_FORCE_DARKEN");
+        if (force_dark != nullptr)
+        {
+            play.rtint_enabled = 1;
+            play.rtint_level = 0;       // <= 0 selects the light branch
+            play.rtint_light = atoi(force_dark);   // negative == darker
+            debug_script_log("DOSAGS_FORCE_DARKEN applied rtint_light=%d",
+                             play.rtint_light);
+        }
+    }
+#endif
+
     set_our_eip(-43);
 
     // Only auto-set first restart point in < 3.6.1 games,
-- 
